senses.gloss:
जल् cl. 1. ˚लति (pf. जजाल, Pāṇ. viii, 4, 54, Sch.), ‘to be rich’ or ‘to cover’ (derived fr. जाल?), Dhātup. xx, 3;
to be sharp, ib.;
to be stiff or dull (for जड्, derived fr. जड), ib. : cl. 10. जालयति, to cover, xxxii, 10.

जल्प् (√ लप् redupl.?) cl. 1. ज॑ल्पति (ep. also Ā. pf. जजल्प, R.) to speak inarticulately, murmur, ŚBr. xi, 5, 1, 4 ;
to chatter, prattle, W.;
to say, speak, converse with (instr. or सार्धम्), MBh.; R. &c.;
to speak about (acc.), MBh. iv, 864; v, 4515;
 = √ अर्च्, to praise, Naigh. iii, 14;
 (said of the Koïl) to sound (its song), Bhartṛ. :
Caus. जल्पयति to cause to speak, Pāṇ. i, 4, 52, Vārtt. 3.
